  "answer": "This has been requested before. The CPU and Memory icons you mean are most likely the stats on the Command Palette Dock, and PowerToys#46434 asks for temperature readings there. That request is still open. A contributor is working on a PR that adds a single heat metric (thermal zone data read through PDH). Windows has no native way to read per-component CPU temperature, so a detailed CPU temp would need vendor-specific drivers or WMI, and that isn't planned. Please follow and upvote #46434. Requests to show CPU temperature in the Windows taskbar itself (#35623, #33966) were closed as duplicates of the taskbar-integration requests #445 and #855. Until a temperature readout ships, a third-party monitor such as Core Temp can show it in the system tray."
 },
